From 01501045785889f265c5aa615cc5f27895674478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yonto-app <336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:51:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vmem: offer the format callback the picture's visible size
Message-Id: <01501045785889f265c5aa615cc5f27895674478.vmem.336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>

A software decoder pads its pictures to the size its code works in, 258
lines for one of 240, and the callback was given that size as the
picture's. A caller that kept it, as the documentation lets it, got the
picture scaled up to it and so out of its shape.
---
 modules/video_output/vmem.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/vmem.c b/modules/video_output/vmem.c
index a046d7c33e..341a59c907 100644
--- a/modules/video_output/vmem.c
+++ b/modules/video_output/vmem.c
@@ -142,6 +142,11 @@ static int Open(vlc_object_t *object)
     if (setup != NULL) {
         char chroma[5];
 
+        /* The picture, not the lines and columns its decoder pads it with,
+         * which the callback would take for the picture's own size. */
+        fmt.i_width = fmt.i_visible_width;
+        fmt.i_height = fmt.i_visible_height;
+
         memcpy(chroma, &fmt.i_chroma, 4);
         chroma[4] = '\0';
         memset(sys->pitches, 0, sizeof(sys->pitches));
-- 
